---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "Families"
---

{% set sidebar_items = [
  { label: "Ancestors", url: "/people/" },
  { label: "Families", url: "/families/" }
] %}

<div class="section-layout">
  {% include "partials/section-sidebar.njk" %}

  <div class="section-content">
    <div class="page-header">
      <h1>Families</h1>
      <p class="page-intro">
        Ancestors documents individual lives — one person, their vital facts, their record trail. Families is where those threads get woven back together: the marriages that joined two lines, the migrations a whole household made together, the mysteries that only make sense when you look at several people at once instead of one.
      </p>
      <p class="page-intro">
        This section is newer than the rest of the site and still mostly unwritten. As entries are finished, they will appear below — pieces on how a Brewster became a Woodruff, on the Bates and Jackson lines finding each other, and on the unresolved question of where the Chaney family truly began. Check back as the research catches up to the outline.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="journal-list">
      {%- for entry in collections.families | reverse %}
      {%- if entry.url != "/families/" %}
      <article class="journal-card">
        <h2 class="journal-card__title">
          <a href="{{ entry.url }}">{{ entry.data.title }}</a>
        </h2>
        {% if entry.data.excerpt %}
        <p class="journal-card__excerpt">{{ entry.data.excerpt }}</p>
        {% endif %}
      </article>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>

    {% if collections.families.length <= 1 %}
    <p class="text-muted text-sans">No family narratives published yet — check back soon.</p>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</div>